# --- COMMIT HELP ---
# Types:
#   feat            (A new feature for the user)
#   fix             (A bug fix)
#   docs            (Documentation only changes, e.g., docs(changelog))
#   style           (Formatting, missing semi-colons, no code change)
#   refactor        (Refactoring code without changing behavior or fixing bugs)
#   perf            (A code change that improves performance)
#   test            (Adding or correcting existing tests)
#   build           (Changes that affect the build system or external dependencies)
#   ci              (Changes to CI configuration files and scripts)
#   chore           (Maintenance, release bumps, tooling, e.g., chore(release))
#   revert          (Reverts a previous commit)
#
# Common Release Scopes:
#   chore(release)   Use when bumping package version & changelog for a new release
#   docs(changelog)  Use when making standalone updates to CHANGELOG.md/release notes
#
# Formatting Rules:
#   * Append `!` after type/scope for breaking changes (e.g., `feat(api)!: drop v1 endpoints`)
#   * Use imperative mood in the description ("add" not "added", "change" not "changes")
#   * Keep description lowercase and do NOT end with a period
#   * Separate summary, body, and footer with blank lines
